      "samples": "{{count}} samples",
      "tokens": "Input / output tokens",
      "na": "N/A",
      "empty": "No model calls in this period",
      "definitionsTitle": "How these are counted",
      "definitions": {
        "attempts": "Attempts: when the primary provider fails and the backup answers, that is two attempts, each under its own model. For paid accounts the OpenAI client may retry up to 2 times inside one attempt (free accounts' calls are not retried automatically); an author pressing Retry is a new attempt; our own quota refusals are not attempts. A successful model call does not mean the writing round finished.",
        "successRate": "Success rate = succeeded ÷ (succeeded + failed + timed out). Cancelled attempts (author stop, disconnect, round time limit, suggestion deadline) and unrecorded ones are left out of the denominator and listed separately.",
        "latency": "Total time: from starting the call to the full reply (stream end for streaming), successful attempts only; for free accounts it also includes the two database transactions that reserve the cost before the call and settle it after. Percentiles are nearest-rank over all samples; the All models row pools the samples instead of averaging models.",
        "ttft": "First token: from starting the call to the first generated content (text, reasoning or tool arguments); events without content, such as the connection opening, do not count, and for free accounts it also includes reserving the cost before the call. Only the streaming writing assistant has it; intent routing, suggestions and polish are not streamed and show N/A.",
        "decode": "Decode speed = total output tokens ÷ total generation time (first token to stream end), not an average of per-call speeds. Output tokens are reported by the provider and include reasoning and tool arguments; if a provider does not stream its reasoning, that time lands in first token and the speed reads high. Calls without reported usage are left out.",
        "notRecorded": "Not recorded: calls from before these metrics, back-filled chat history (one row per round) and material breakdown have no outcome or timing; they count toward attempts, tokens and cost, but not the success rate, and never as zero. Failed and cancelled attempts rarely report usage, so tokens and cost are a lower bound."
      }
    },
